# Paths viki should not index. One glob per line; `#` comments.
# A pattern with no `/` matches any path COMPONENT; one with `/` matches the
# whole path relative to the indexed root, and also everything beneath it.
#
# Why this file exists, measured 2026-08-24: 83.4% of this repo's chunks were
# vendored SQLCipher/LibreSSL source copied in for the wasm build, 8.6% was
# build output, and 6.9% was actually this project. A question about why ndvss
# was chosen over sqlite-vec returned a vendored sqlite3.c at RANK 1.
# SKIP_DIRS in viki_index.c matches by BASENAME, so `vendor-wasm` is not
# `vendor` and `dist` is not `build`.

# vendored third-party source -- not ours, and it drowns everything
edge/vendor-wasm
edge/dist
vendor

# build products
build/dist
build/obj
build/libobj
*.o
*.a
*.wasm

# a demonstration artifact, not a decision -- 44KB of CSS/JS whose chunks would
# be corpus noise. What it demonstrates is argued in CALENDAR_DESIGN_V2.md,
# which IS indexed.
experiments/calendar-interchange-prototype.html

# the derived cache itself
.viki
